        "body": "closes: #XXXX\r\n<!-- If there is no issue number make sure to describe clearly *why* this PR is necessary. -->\r\n\r\n### This PR:\r\n* Added detailed documentation for the `RescuePRFCore` structure, explaining its role and purpose.\r\n* Enhanced comments for the methods `full_state_keyed_sponge_with_zero_padding` and `full_state_keyed_sponge_no_padding`, including:\r\n  - Description of arguments\r\n  - Explanation of return values\r\n  - Conditions for possible errors\r\n* Expanded documentation for the public `RescuePRF` structure, providing:\r\n  - Implementation parameters (fixed input/output lengths)\r\n  - Key size\r\n  - Cryptographic primitives used\r\n\r\n### This PR does not:\r\n* Introduce new features or modify existing functionality beyond the documentation and comments.\r\n* Implement tests for features outside the scope of these documentation improvements.\r\n\r\n### Key places to review:\r\n* `RescuePRFCore` structure for its updated documentation.\r\n* `full_state_keyed_sponge_with_zero_padding` and `full_state_keyed_sponge_no_padding` methods for new comments and clarifications.\r\n* `RescuePRF` structure documentation for completeness and accuracy.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nBefore we can merge this PR, please make sure that all the following items have been\r\nchecked off. If any of the checklist items are not applicable, please leave them but\r\nwrite a little note why.\r\n\r\n- [ ] Targeted PR against correct branch (main)\r\n- [ ] Linked to GitHub issue with discussion and accepted design OR have an explanation in the PR that describes this work.\r\n- [ ] Wrote unit tests (if applicable)\r\n- [ ] Updated relevant documentation in the code\r\n- [ ] Added relevant changelog entries to the `CHANGELOG.md` of touched crates.\r\n- [ ] Re-reviewed `Files changed` in the GitHub PR explorer\r\n\r\n",
