        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "#### Description\r\nExpect.To should have methods allowing type validation:\r\n- `BeType<T>()` / `BeType(type)` - exact type match\r\n- `BeAssignableFrom<T>()` / `BeAssignableFrom(type)` - equivalent of `Type.IsAssignableFrom`\r\n- `BeAssignableTo<T>()` / `BeAssignableTo(type)` - equivalent of `Type.IsAssignableTo`\r\n- `BeCastableTo<T>()` / `BeCastableTo(type)` - (if possible) given type can be casted to T, including implicit and explicit casts (passed as params)\r\n- `BeCastableFrom<T>()` / `BeCastableFrom(type)` - (if possible) T can be casted to given type, including implicit and explicit casts (passed as params)\r\n\r\n#### Progress\r\n<!-- This section should be updated during development, not reporting an issue. Add more steps as needed. -->\r\n- [ ] Feature is implemented,\r\n- [ ] Ensured backward-compatibility,\r\n- [ ] Ensured good debugging experience",
